mmander-in-chief  as you know we've inherited quite a  budget crunch from president trump  shortly after trump's election to the  presidency the show referenced its own  uncanny prediction with the chalkboard  gag in which bart writes being right  sucks many of bart's chalkboard quotes  are peppered with evocative innuendos  and playful puns  he apparently couldn't stop talking  about the 12-inch pianist  in marge be not proud and makes a nod to  sir mix-a-lot when he notes  sherry does not got back in wild bart's  can't be broken  among some of his more colorful  innuendos you've got bart vowing not to  hang donuts on his person  promising not to make fun of cupid's  dink and acknowledging that  pork is not a verb bart also shares some  of his rejected words of wisdom in 101  mitigations  when he is seen writing chili fries do  not go in like a lamb  and out like a lion but things get taken  to the next level during the opening  sequence for the episode pray anything  in which bart scribbles out spongebob is  not a contraceptive  gotta give the kid credit for creativity  don't you  bart certainly gets up to his fair share  of shenanigans and if the show's  chalkboard gags are anything to go by  they don't all happen on screen  over the years some of bart's  prank-based chalkboards have included i  will not yell fire in a crowded  classroom  i will not yell she's dead during roll  call and the pledge of allegiance does  not end with hale satan  he apparently harassed a blind person by  promising to return the seeing eye dog  in whacking day  and vowed he wouldn't put hot sauce in  the cpr dummy at the start of father  knows worst  bart has also expressed a rather more  worrying side to his classroom antics  including writing five days is not too  long to wait for a gun  non-flammable is not a challenge and  hooligan is not a profession  one of bart's most notable moments of  chalkboard mischief hails from the  episode  doe canada bart writes ha-ha on the  blackboard  then hits it which rotates to reveal  nelson tape to the other side  who's laughing now the writers on the  simpsons are no strangers to getting  meta and this  is usually most noticeable during the  show's opening sequences  and of course the chalkboard gags for  example there's the time when bart cut  corners while writing i will not cut  corners by  only writing the line out six times and  filling out the remaining lines with  ditto quotation marks  he also slyly remarks this punishment is  not boring and pointless in camp crusty  and writes i'm sorry i broke the  blackboard on a whiteboard in black eyed  please  in reference to how critics described  south park when it first aired bart  writes i'm not charlie brown on acid  in the blunder years he also poked fun  at the simpsons itself by writing i will  not celebrate meaningless milestones  when the show was airing its 100th  episode  after butterfinger canceled their  simpsons ad campaign because the brand  had been the butt of some of the show's  jokes bart responded by writing i will  not bite the hand that feeds me  butterfingers  then when the simpsons hit the big  screen and got their own movie in 2007  bart promised not to illegally download  this movie in its intro  he also joked that he will never win an  emmy in homer's barbershop quartet  even though by that point the show had  already won nine  throughout 2020 the united states and  the rest of the world faced the first  waves of the kovit 19 pandemic  seemingly overnight countless people  found themselves struggling to adapt to  a new way of life  in an attempt to stem the tide many  offices went virtual  and so did schools parents everywhere  suddenly found themselves trying to help  their children navigate  online classrooms and curricula and from  the looks of it not even the simpsons  were immune to the chaos of the  coronavirus pandemic  as a way to honor these drastic changes  the simpsons modified its chalkboard gag  for an episode that aired on april 19th  2020. during the intro to the incredible  lightness of being a baby bart's  classroom is empty and a single line on  the board reads  school online a poignant nod to the  dramatic events that would have  resonated with students parents and  teachers everywhere  ralph wiggum is one of the simpsons  stranger and most endearing characters  sure he's a perfectly sweet little boy  but he's also incredibly odd and  about as brainless as you can get that's  where i saw the leprechaun  right a leprechaun he told me to burn  things  of course bart is well aware of ralph's  many quirks and is constantly teasing  him for it even during the show's  chalkboard gags  in the intro to fear of flying bart  writes ralph won't morph if you squeeze  him hard enough  a reference to the color morphing stress  balls that were popular at the time the  show aired  one of bart's more savage notes  concerning his odd classmate can be seen  in apocalypse cow  in which he writes a person's a person  no matter how ralph  class pets are a fun way to reinforce  the lessons they're taught in school  as well as help students experience the  responsibility of taking care of a small  life  in fact studies have also shown that  pets in the classroom have positive  impacts on student behavior  enhanced social interaction and student  attitudes  not that you'd know it looking at bart  those poor  poor hamsters there have been a handful  of class hamsters featured on the  simpsons over the years  including nibbles the hamster who  bravely helped save those trapped inside  the school in skinner's sense of snow  and even made it to space and back in  she of little faith  regardless of their heroism however bart  has relentlessly mocked his class  hamsters during the show's chalkboard  gags  during the intro to homer the whopper  bart writes the class hamster isn't just  sleeping  and in day of the jack and apes he notes  the hamster did not have a full life  yikes get in that ball and run for the  hills little hamster  godspeed nibbles godspeed  nuts being a parent is a massive  blessing but it can also be incredibly  frustrating and having a kid like bart  must make it even harder to exercise  discipline still that doesn't exactly  excuse homer's particular approach to  parenting  that is strangling bart whenever he  loses his patience  luckily this is just a cartoon which  generally makes homer's strangulations  more humorous than horrific  still this is one aspect of the show  that hasn't aged too well over the last  30 years and even though it's set in the  context of the show's off-the-wall humor  it can still be a tough pill to swallow  and this problem is eloquently touched  upon during the chalkboard gag for frank  gets testy in which homer can be seen  writing strangling  is not an effective parenting tool as a  smug bart watches on  during the show's time on television the  simpsons has stirred up plenty of  controversy surrounding religion  one obvious example of this is ned  flanders who is a constant target for  jokes about christianity  but one of the more subtle ways the show  has poked fun at religion over various  episodes  is through the use of barch chalkboard  quotes in the intro to  the burns and the bees bart writes jesus  is not mad his birthday is on christmas  and  in reality bites he notes there was no  roman god named farticus  but one of his darkest and funniest  remarks comes during the intro to dark  knight court in which bart writes  jesus's last words were not tgif  in a world like the simpsons mothers are  the cornerstones of their households and  that goes doubly for marge simpson  mom you're always trying to give me  potatoes what is it with you  i just think they're neat but even  though marge loves bart unconditionally  he can definitely make things difficult  at times just take his attitude to  mother's day for example  over the years bart has lambasted that  particular holiday by writing things  such as today is not mothra's day  eating my vegetables is not a mother's  day present and dirty clothes are not a  mother's day gift  in the intro to homer scissorhands he  even writes i do not deserve a mother's  day gift for being one badass mother  but hey maybe it's not all that bad  during the intro to ned and edna's blend  in one of his more lucid moments bart  writes call your mother during the  commercials  during the 25th season of the simpsons  executive producer  al jean dropped a massive bombshell on  fans that in the near future they'd be  killing off a major character  the writers had initially planned for  the death to take place later that  season  but in the end they had to delay it  until the show's 26th season  this delay only stirred the public's  interest that much more and for months  simpsons fans were left in a state of  deep suspense furious speculation and  rumors circulated across the  internet over who exactly the unlucky  soul would be  many suspected krusty the clown as being  the doomed character  but when the episode clown in the dumps  finally did air it turned out his father  rabbi hyman krastovski was the  long-hinted character who  would ultimately pass away playing up to  fans speculation about the long-awaited  episode the show opens with an equally  memorable chalkboard gag  in his typical ruthless fashion bart  rights spoiler alert unfortunately my  dad doesn't die  another major simpsons character who  passed away on the show is bart's  teacher edna krabappel  during season 25 the actor who voiced  the character marcia wallace passed away  as a humble way of paying respect to  wallace's memory bart's normally savage  tone was tamed for the chalkboard gag  opening the episode following wallace's  passing  in four regrettings and a funeral a  solemn looking bart  writes just one line on the chalkboard  we'll really miss you mrs k  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

